{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/845854-the-double-edged-rpg-system","id":845854,"title":"The Double Edged RPG System","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-11T15:57:48-08:00","id":845854,"title":"The Double Edged RPG System","content":"Okay I've begun building my own RPG game system which I call the double Edge System RPG Game System.<br /> <br /> The basic idea I had for it is instead of rolling for stats or somekind of point buy, Stats go from 10 to -10 with each end of the spectrem being benificial.<br /> <br /> And your basic biological/Spiritual choices for Stats are based on Species, then you pick Backgrounds with their own Stats, Education System with its own Stats(which are like classes), and Hobbies (kind of like merits and feats, but their Stats that don't fit into the other Catogories).<br /> <br /> So stats come with resource pools.<br /> <br /> So Character X Takes Human.<br /> <br /> X gains the stats Muscular System (+Heavy/Lean-), Brain (Left Hemisphere/Right Hemisphere), Respatory System (Breath/Blood), Reproductive System (Male/Female), Symmetry (+Beautiful/Ugly-), Nervous System (+Sensitive/Numb-), Sense Organs (+Audio/Visual-), Soul (+Sacred/Profane-), Health (+Alive/Undead-)<br /> <br /> A different Species has its own physical and Spiritual Anatomy and will have a mix of different and the same stats.<br /> <br /> Then Background will grant a couple of Skills tied to your personal history and/or Nationality.<br /> <br /> So for example Canadian might have the Patriot Stat (+Nationalist/Rebel-) and Lingual (+Bilingual/Monolingual-).<br /> <br /> Then comes Education Tracks. Possible Education Tracks include various Trades, Natural Sciences (regular sciences + Philosphy), Social Sciences, Arcanology (wizards), Theology, Anthropology (Hybred class between Social and Natural Sciences), Military Tactics, Arts, The Streets.<br /> <br /> So Someone who takes Arcanology might start off with Spells: Energy (Force/Effiency), Spells: Summoning (+Power/Duration-), Arcane Knowledge (+Bredth/Depth-), Spells: Probablity Manipulation, (+Buff/Debuff-). As the Character gains experience they can pick new skills within their Education Track or go Multidisplinary and begin a new Education Track.<br /> <br /> Finally there are Hobbies which are stats that don't fit in the other catogories or attempts to dabble beyond your normal choices. You gain hobbies usually say once every 3 or 5 levels (haven't decided). Some Education Tracks (ETs) may offer electives at certain levels were you can choose from a subset of hobbies outside your normal hobby gains.<br /> <br /> There will be different types of hitpoints depending on species. Example Humans have Health Points which one wants to keep from hitting zero, which is death/destructuon (but -HP isn't bad, it just means your an undead human, things that damage you add +hp instead of -hp like on a human). Other Species, like say a Species of Energy Beings or Mechanical ones will have a different Health Stat, which will grant a different Health resource pool.<br /> <br /> Each Stat offers access to different actions. Respatory System grants access to breathing, which hypothetical mechanical species usually won't need or benifit from.<br /> <br /> I picture a possible character sheet having a section for personal information (like your name), a section for Species Stats, a Section for Background Stats, a Section for ETs Stats, a Section for Hobbies Stats. Each Stat section would have a slot to write down the name of the Stat, a 10 to -10 scale, and a box to write down any resource pool that comes with it, if it comed with one, most won't.<br /> <br /> This is still a work in progress, but feedback would be welcome. <br /> <br /> PS I'm toying with idea Items could come with their own Stats, but have prerequist Stats to use them. Like an Energy Being wouldn't have the muscular system stat so couldn't use Warhammer Item unless it found away to gain one (like a weird hobby or an exotic item).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T16:14:25-08:00","id":845860,"title":"","content":"The Character is assumed to have all the basic equiptment, like a pair of pants, that their species would be expected to have, and all the basic equiptment needed to use their Stats. Actual Items with Stats are special, like Magic Warhammer or a Customized AK 47, or or the Explosive Regenerating Testicles of Dead Alien Brood King, or a Quantum Sigularity Launcher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T16:23:04-08:00","id":845864,"title":"","content":"I also have an ideal for a First Setting for the Double Edged RPG System (DERS).<br /> <br /> Multiverse Corp with a dark series of Partnerships, picked an uninhabited Parrell Earth and Colonized it/Transformed it into a massive Pyschotic Theme Park, filled with wonders and horrors, Magical, Mundane, Shear Horrifying, Spiritual, and Sci-Fi. And turned the Moon into Connected Resort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T09:06:52-08:00","id":846105,"title":"","content":"For the conflict resolution system I haven't decided between dice or diceless. I'm leaning towards dice as most people will be familiar with that.<br /> <br /> Maybe you start with a Dice Pool of +5 and add or subtract dice based on the Stats invovled.<br /> <br /> So punching someone starts at a pool of +5 and has a Muscular of +6 (heavy muscles), he adds six dice to the pool. His Target chooses the tense up action in response, which relies on the nervous system stat which has -7 nervous system (numb) so he subtracts 7 from the dice pool.<br /> <br /> If he had +7 (sensitive) instead, tensing up would be a bad idea as that would add +7 to the dice pool of the character trying to hit him.<br /> <br /> I leaning towards -stats being more defence, dropping a target number for required for success and debuffing stats, with some exceptions. <br /> <br /> +stats would be more adding dice, buffing, and adding to the target number required to hit or manipulate them, plus other stuff.<br /> <br /> For combat and other contested actions I'm thinking that you can take primary action once per round, and a defence action once every time your attacks or some takes a primary action that you can oppose. I might limit the amount of defence actions that can be taken in a turn. Also the stat one uses to defend themselves depends on the defence action, tensing up uses the nervious system, praying for salvation (a theology stat action) uses Divine Temperment stat (+Wrathful, -Peaceful) and dodge uses Muscular System (+heavy, Lean- with lean helping you dodge) for example.<br /> <br /> As for ETs I'm thinking of limiting ETs to three per character max.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T09:16:40-08:00","id":846116,"title":"","content":"______________________________________<br /> | Personal Information |<br /> |_____________________________________|<br /> |Background | Hobbies |<br /> |______________|_______________________| | ET 1 |ET 2 | ET3 <br /> | | | <br /> <br /> This is the basic design I have in my mind for the character sheet, very, very perliminary.","signature":"______________________________________<br /> | Personal Information |<br /> |_____________________________________|<br /> |Background | Hobbies |<br /> |______________|_______________________| | ET 1 |ET 2 | ET3 <br /> | | | <br /> <br /> This is the basic design I have in my mind for the character sheet, very, very perliminary.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}